WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
Hello and welcome back to JD Science.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.640
Today we are exploring photosynthesis.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:10.340
Plants use carbon dioxide and water with energy from sunlight

4
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.220
and chlorophyll to make glucose and oxygen.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.060
Carbon dioxide enters through the stomata.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.500
Water travels up from the roots.

7
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.080
The equation is 6 carbon dioxide plus 6 water gives

8
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.080
glucose plus 6 oxygen.

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.080
Glucose can be respiration converted into starch

10
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.260
for storage made into cellulose for cell walls combined

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.340
with nitrates to make amino acids or converted into lipids

12
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.000
for seeds.

13
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.020
The rate of photosynthesis depends on temperature, intensity and

14
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.860
carbon dioxide concentration.

15
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.160
Enzymes can become denatured at high temperatures.

16
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.600
Light intensity falls off with distance by the inverse square law.

17
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.900
Doubling the distance cuts the intensity to a quarter.

18
00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.280
The balanced symbol equation is 6 carbon dioxide molecules

19
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.260
plus 6 water molecules producing 1 molecule and

20
00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.140
6 oxygen molecules using light energy.

21
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.480
A limiting factor is the condition in shortest supply relative to

22
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.340
the plant's needs.

23
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.760
Increasing light will not keep increasing the rate if carbon dioxide

24
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:23.100
or temperature can

25
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.680
be treated as a point source and other conditions are controlled.

26
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.940
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

27
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:31.840
your own words.

28
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:36.120
Focus on what happens, why it happens and how the structures

29
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.160
involved help the process work.

30
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.400
Now pause the video and try this exam style question.

31
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.940
A plant is moved from 20 cm to 40 cm from

32
00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.360
a lamp.

33
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:51.000
Explain how the light intensity changes and what

34
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.080
this does to the rate of photosynthesis.

35
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.200
Here is a model answer.

36
00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.560
Doubling the distance reduces the light intensity to a quarter so

37
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.340
the rate of photosynthesis falls because light is limiting the

38
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:03.640
rate.

39
